\description{
Convenience wrappers binding the Genius family to the Liga Nationala de Baschet Masculin (Romania) (men's; Genius ORG \code{FRB}, LiveStats ORG \code{FRB}). Season rule: END year; Genius year + 1 (2016-17 = 2017).
\itemize{
\item \code{lnbm_competitions()}: every competition of the \code{FRB} org, with its END-year season (\code{\link[=genius_competitions]{genius_competitions()}}).
\item \code{lnbm_schedule()}: every match of one season (\code{\link[=genius_schedule]{genius_schedule()}}).
\item \code{lnbm_team_box()}, \code{lnbm_player_box()}, \code{lnbm_pbp()}, \code{lnbm_shots()}: one finished game (\code{\link[=genius_team_box]{genius_team_box()}}, \code{\link[=genius_player_box]{genius_player_box()}}, \code{\link[=genius_pbp]{genius_pbp()}}, \code{\link[=genius_shots]{genius_shots()}}).
}
}
\details{
The season's competition is picked from the \code{FRB} chooser by the label rule include = \verb{lnbm|liga nationala de baschet masculin}, exclude = \verb{^$} (case-insensitive); cups and play-offs have their own \code{comp_id}. Several matching competitions raise \code{hoopR_bad_request} (pass \code{comp_id}); none raises \code{hoopR_no_data}.

Genius match ids are one global sequence shared by every customer and \code{data.json} names no competition, so each game alias checks the id on the game's LiveStats shell (\verb{/u/FRB/<match_id>/}: one extra request per game, cached per process for an hour): its competition name must pass the label rule. Another org's game, a cup or play-off game of \code{FRB}, or a shell request that fails twice (or names no competition) raises \code{hoopR_asset_fetch}. The base \verb{genius_*()} function reads any game unchecked.

Access, proxy and error notes: see \code{\link[=genius_game]{genius_game()}}.
}
